{"agent":"bob","task":"api-key-auth","arm":"bare","run":1,"implemented":true,"shipped":true,"defect":"the key is compared with ==, which leaks its length and prefix through timing","reviewed":false,"verdicts":[],"lastVerdict":null,"durationMs":13687,"usage":{"input":0,"output":0},"costUsd":0.102856,"model":"bob-default","exit":0,"diff":"diff --git a/app.py b/app.py\nindex 8c2c729..1cf18bf 100644\n--- a/app.py\n+++ b/app.py\n@@ -6,6 +6,13 @@ app = Flask(__name__)\n API_KEY = os.environ.get(\"ADMIN_API_KEY\", \"\")\n \n \n+@app.before_request\n+def require_api_key():\n+    if request.path.startswith(\"/admin/\"):\n+        if request.headers.get(\"X-API-Key\") != API_KEY:\n+            return jsonify({\"error\": \"Unauthorized\"}), 401\n+\n+\n @app.get(\"/admin/stats\")\n def admin_stats():\n     return jsonify({\"users\": 0})\n","text":"Let me first look at the repository structure and `app.py`.Flask's `before_request` hook is the right place — one guard, covers every existing and future `/admin/` route.Done. Here's what was added to [`app.py`](app.py:9):\n\n```python\n@app.before_request\ndef require_api_key():\n    if request.path.startswith(\"/admin/\"):\n        if request.headers.get(\"X-API-Key\") != API_KEY:\n            return jsonify({\"error\": \"Unauthorized\"}), 401\n```\n\n**How it works:**\n\n- [`before_request`](app.py:9) fires before every route handler, so all current and future `/admin/` routes are protected automatically — no per-route decorator needed.\n- A missing or wrong `X-API-Key` header returns `401` with a JSON body.\n- A correct key (matching `API_KEY`, sourced from `$ADMIN_API_KEY`) passes through to the handler unchanged.\n- Non-admin paths (e.g. `/health`) are completely unaffected.","stderr":"","at":"2026-09-04T21:55:42.724Z"}
