rs handle it identically to before. No new input surface.\n\n3. **Errors.** No swallowed exceptions. Dict key access on a row we just pulled from `ROWS` cannot `KeyError` unless `ROWS` is missing `role` — but every entry in `ROWS` carries `role`. The `None` path is unchanged.\n\n4. **Off-diff changes.** None.\n\n5. **Dependencies.** None added.\n\n6. **Trust boundaries.** `role` sourced from internal `ROWS`, not from the request. No injection surface, no secrets, no PII beyond what existed.\n\n7. **Tests.** No test harness exists in the repo. Not a regression introduced here.\n\n8. **Rollback.** Revert + deploy. No migration.\n\n9. **Observability.** No new log lines needed; no change to error paths.\n\n10. **Naming/dead code.** Docstring updated on `users.py:1`. No dead code.\n\n```\nGRUMP: APPROVE — users.py, api.py, reports.py\nFine.\n```","stderr":"","at":"2026-09-05T05:11:39.522Z"}
