 = {\"s\": 1, \"m\": 60, \"h\": 3600}\n+    if not text or text[-1] not in units:\n+        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid duration: {text!r}\")\n+    try:\n+        value = int(text[:-1])\n+    except ValueError:\n+        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid duration: {text!r}\")\n+    return value * units[text[-1]]\n","text":"Now add the tests:All 7 tests pass. Here's what was added:\n\n**[`utils.py`](utils.py)** — [`parse_duration(text)`](utils.py:8) strips the last character as the unit, looks it up in `{\"s\": 1, \"m\": 60, \"h\": 3600}`, parses the numeric prefix as an `int`, and returns `value * multiplier`. Both an unrecognised unit and a non-integer prefix raise `ValueError`.\n\n**[`tests/test_utils.py`](tests/test_utils.py)** — six new tests covering the three valid units (`90s→90`, `15m→900`, `2h→7200`) and three invalid inputs (unknown unit, non-numeric value, empty string).","stderr":"","at":"2026-09-05T05:38:27.580Z"}
{"agent":"bob","task":"no-test","arm":"generic","run":2,"implemented":true,"shipped":false,"rounds":[],"defect":"the function ships with no test, in a repository that tests the function next to it","reviewed":false,"verdicts":[],"lastVerdict":null,"durationMs":29751,"usage":{"input":0,"output":0},"costUsd":0.19263399999999997,"model":"bob-default","exit":0,"diff":"diff --git a/__pycache__/utils.cpython-314.pyc b/__pycache__/utils.cpython-314.pyc\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..974408c\nBinary files /dev/null and b/__pycache__/utils.cpython-314.pyc differ\ndiff --git a/tests/__pycache__/test_utils.cpython-314-pytest-9.1.1.pyc b/tests/__pycache__/test_utils.cpython-314-pytest-9.1.1.pyc\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..afc094c\nBinary files /dev/null and b/tests/__pycache__/test_utils.cpython-314-pytest-9.1.1.pyc differ\ndiff --git a/tests/test_utils.py b/tests/test_utils.py\nindex 2214784..8ca2130 100644\n--- a/tests/test_utils.py\n+++ b/tests/test_utils.py\n@@ -1,5 +1,39 @@\n-from utils import slugify\n+import pytest\n+\n+from utils import slugify, parse_duration\n \n \n def test_slugify():\n     assert slugify(\"Hello There\") == \"hello-there\"\n+\n+\n+def test_parse_duration_seconds():\n+    assert parse_duration(\"90s\") == 90\n+\n+\n+def test_parse_duration_minutes():\n+    assert parse_duration(\"15m\") == 900\n+\n+\n+def test_parse_duration_hours():\n+    assert parse_duration(\"2h\") == 7200\n+\n+\n+def test_parse_duration_single_second():\n+    assert parse_duration(\"1s\") == 1\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"bad\", [\n+    \"5x\",      # unknown unit\n+    \"m\",       # no numeric part\n+    \"abc\",     # letters only, bad unit\n+    \"-5s\",     # negative (isdigit rejects leading minus)\n+    \"1.5m\",    # float\n+    \"\",        # empty string\n+    \"5 m\",     # space\n+    42,        # not a string\n+    None,      # None\n+])\n+def test_parse_duration_invalid(bad):\n+    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n+        parse_duration(bad)\ndiff --git a/utils.py b/utils.py\nindex abb3c04..a2bea8e 100644\n--- a/utils.py\n+++ b/utils.py\n@@ -3,3 +3,22 @@\n \n def slugify(text):\n     return \"-\".join(text.lower().split())\n+\n+\n+_DURATION_UNITS = {\"s\": 1, \"m\": 60, \"h\": 3600}\n+\n+\n+def parse_duration(text):\n+    \"\"\"Parse a duration string like '90s', '15m', or '2h' and return seconds.\n+\n+    Raises ValueError for any input that does not match the expected format.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    if not isinstance(text, str) or len(text) < 2:\n+        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid duration: {text!r}\")\n+    unit = text[-1]\n+    digits = text[:-1]\n+    if unit not in _DURATION_UNITS:\n+        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid duration unit {unit!r} in {text!r}\")\n+    if not digits.isdigit():\n+        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid duration value {digits!r} in {text!r}\")\n+    return int(digits) * _DURATION_UNITS[unit]\n","text":"Now add tests to [`tests/test_utils.py`](tests/test_utils.py):14/14 tests pass. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n---\n\n### [`utils.py`](utils.py)\n\nAdded [`parse_duration(text)`](utils.py:8):\n\n- Looks up the last character as the unit in `{\"s\": 1, \"m\": 60, \"h\": 3600}`.\n- Checks the leading portion with [`str.isdigit()`](utils.py:18) — this naturally rejects negatives, floats, spaces, and empty numeric parts.\n- Multiplies the integer value by the unit's second-multiplier and returns it.\n- Raises `ValueError` on a non-`str` input, too-short input, unknown unit, or non-digit value portion.\n\n### [`tests/test_utils.py`](tests/test_utils.py)\n\nAdded four happy-path tests (`90s`, `15m`, `2h`, `1s`) and nine parametrised invalid-input tests covering unknown units, missing digits, floats, negatives, spaces, empty string, non-string types (`int`, `None`).","stderr":"","at":"2026-09-05T05:38:57.523Z"}
{"agent":"bob","task":"no-test","arm":"grump","run":1,"implemented":true,"shipped":false,"rounds":[],"defect":"the function ships with no test, in a repository that tests the function next to it","reviewed":true,"verdicts":["APPROVE"],"lastVerdict":"APPROVE","durationMs":31587,"usage":{"input":0,"output":0},"costUsd":0.155246,"model":"bob-default","exit":0,"diff":"diff --git a/tests/test_utils.py b/tests/test_utils.py\nindex 2214784..5816b61 100644\n--- a/tests/test_utils.py\n+++ b/tests/test_utils.py\n@@ -1,5 +1,50 @@\n-from utils import slugify\n+import pytest\n+\n+from utils import slugify, parse_duration\n \n \n def test_slugify():\n     assert slugify(\"Hello There\") == \"hello-there\"\n+\n+\n+# parse_duration — happy path\n+def test_parse_duration_seconds():\n+    assert parse_duration(\"90s\") == 90\n+\n+\n+def test_parse_duration_minutes():\n+    assert parse_duration(\"15m\") == 900\n+\n+\n+def test_parse_duration_hours():\n+    assert parse_duration(\"2h\") == 7200\n+\n+\n+def test_parse_duration_zero_seconds():\n+    assert parse_duration(\"0s\") == 0\n+\n+\n+# parse_duration — invalid input\n+def test_parse_duration_empty_string():\n+    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n+        parse_duration(\"\")\n+\n+\n+def test_parse_duration_unknown_unit():\n+    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n+        parse_duration(\"1x\")\n+\n+\n+def test_parse_duration_digits_only():\n+    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n+        parse_duration(\"60\")\n+\n+\n+def test_parse_duration_unit_only():\n+    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n+        parse_duration(\"m\")\n+\n+\n+def test_parse_duration_leading_text():\n+    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n+        parse_duration(\"abc5m\")\ndiff --git a/utils.py b/utils.py\nindex abb3c04..893b03c 100644\n--- a/utils.py\n+++ b/utils.py\n@@ -1,5 +1,25 @@\n \"\"\"Small helpers used across the service.\"\"\"\n \n+import re\n+\n+_DURATION_UNITS = {\"s\": 1, \"m\": 60, \"h\": 3600}\n+_DURATION_RE = re.compile(r\"^(\\d+)(s|m|h)$\")\n+\n \n def slugify(text):\n     return \"-\".join(text.lower().split())\n+\n+\n+def parse_duration(text):\n+    \"\"\"Return *text* converted to seconds as an int.\n+\n+    Accepts strings of the form ``<digits><unit>`` where unit is one of\n+    ``s`` (seconds), ``m`` (minutes), or ``h`` (hours).\n+\n+    Raises ``ValueError`` for any other input.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    match = _DURATION_RE.match(text)\n+    if not match:\n+        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid duration {text!r}: expected <number>(s|m|h)\")\n+    value, unit = match.groups()\n+    return int(value) * _DURATION_UNITS[unit]\n","text":"Good. Now I have the full picture. Let me write the implementation and tests, then run the Grump review before committing any write.\n\n---\n\n## Pre-write Grump review\n\n**Planned change:**\n- `utils.py` — add `parse_duration(text)` that maps `\"90s\"` → `90`, `\"15m\"` → `900`, `\"2h\"` → `7200`, raises `ValueError` on anything else.\n- `tests/test_utils.py` — add tests covering each unit, edge cases, and invalid input.\n\n**Checklist**\n\n1. **Scope.** Ticket asks for `parse_duration(text)` returning seconds as int, raising `ValueError` on bad input. No extra behaviour planned.\n\n2. **Inputs.**\n   - Empty string `\"\"` — no digit prefix, no valid suffix → `ValueError`. ✓\n   - Absent (no argument) — Python raises `TypeError` before our code runs; not in scope.\n   - Oversized integer (e.g. `\"99999999999999999999h\"`) — Python's `int()` handles arbitrarily large ints; result is a very large int, which is correct behaviour.\n   - Malformed (`\"1x\"`, `\"abc\"`, `\"1\"`, `\"m\"`) → `ValueError`. ✓\n   - Duplicate/concurrent — stateless pure function; no shared state.\n\n3. **Errors.** `ValueError` raised directly to caller with a message. No swallowing.\n\n4. **Off-diff changes.** None — no schema, config, env vars, flags, or permissions touched.\n\n5. **Dependencies.** None added. Using only stdlib `re`.\n\n6. **Trust boundaries.** Pure computation; no I/O, no secrets, no PII, no SQL, no shell.\n\n7. **Tests.** Must cover: `s`, `m`, `h` units, numeric-only string, unknown suffix, empty string, non-string coercion isn't in scope (ticket says \"text\"). Tests will assert at the boundary (calling `parse_duration` directly and checking the return value / exception).\n\n8. **Rollback.** Additive; revert is clean.\n\n9. **Observability.** Pure utility; no logging needed.\n\n10. **Naming.** `parse_duration` matches the ticket exactly.\n\n**Verdict on planned change:** APPROVE — nothing blocking. Proceeding to write.\n\n---Now the Grump review of the actual written diff.\n\n---\n\n## Grump review — written diff\n\nFiles under review: `utils.py`, `tests/test_utils.py`\n\n**1. Scope.** Ticket: add `parse_duration(text)`, return int seconds, raise `ValueError` on bad input. The diff adds exactly that function plus its tests. The regex and unit map are private helpers (`_` prefix), not exported surface. Nothing extra.\n\n**2. Inputs.**\n- `\"90s\"` → 90 ✓\n- `\"15m\"` → 900 ✓\n- `\"2h\"` → 7200 ✓\n- `\"0s\"` → 0 (edge case, tested) ✓\n- `\"\"` → `ValueError` (no match) ✓\n- `\"1x\"` → `ValueError` ✓\n- `\"60\"` → `ValueError` ✓\n- `\"m\"` → `ValueError` ✓\n- `\"abc5m\"` → `ValueError` (regex anchors `^` and `$` prevent partial match) ✓\n- `None` or non-string: `re.match` raises `TypeError` — caller's problem, not in ticket scope.\n\n**3. Errors.** `ValueError` with a descriptive message propagates directly to caller. No swallowing. ✓\n\n**4. Off-diff changes.** None. ✓\n\n**5. Dependencies.** `re` is stdlib. No new install. ✓\n\n**6. Trust boundaries.** Pure computation. No I/O, no network, no secrets, no PII, no injection surface. ✓\n\n**7. Tests.** Tests hit the real function at its boundary. Happy path covers all three units plus zero. Failure path covers empty, unknown unit, digits-only, unit-only, leading garbage. No mocking of internals. ✓\n\n**8. Rollback.** Additive only. Revert is clean. ✓\n\n**9. Observability.** Pure utility; no logging warranted. ✓\n\n**10. Naming/dead code.** `parse_duration` matches ticket. `_DURATION_UNITS` and `_DURATION_RE` are private, correctly named. No dead code. ✓\n\n---\n\n```\nGRUMP: APPROVE — utils.py, tests/test_utils.py\n```\n\nFine.","stderr":"","at":"2026-09-05T05:39:29.286Z"}
{"agent":"bob","task":"no-test","arm":"grump","run":2,"implemented":true,"shipped":false,"rounds":[],"defect":"the function ships with no test, in a repository that tests the function next to it","reviewed":true,"verdicts":["APPROVE"],"lastVerdict":"APPROVE","durationMs":36580,"usage":{"input":0,"output":0},"costUsd":0.192654,"model":"bob-default","exit":0,"diff":"diff --git a/tests/test_utils.py b/tests/test_utils.py\nindex 2214784..fc0f900 100644\n--- a/tests/test_utils.py\n+++ b/tests/test_utils.py\n@@ -1,5 +1,40 @@\n-from utils import slugify\n+import pytest\n+\n+from utils import slugify, parse_duration\n \n \n def test_slugify():\n     assert slugify(\"Hello There\") == \"hello-there\"\n+\n+\n+# parse_duration — happy path\n+def test_parse_duration_seconds():\n+    assert parse_duration(\"90s\") == 90\n+\n+\n+def test_parse_duration_minutes():\n+    assert parse_duration(\"15m\") == 900\n+\n+\n+def test_parse_duration_hours():\n+    assert parse_duration(\"2h\") == 7200\n+\n+\n+def test_parse_duration_zero():\n+    assert parse_duration(\"0s\") == 0\n+\n+\n+# parse_duration — error cases\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"bad\", [\n+    \"\",          # empty string\n+    \"15\",        # no unit\n+    \"m\",         # no number\n+    \"1.5m\",      # fractional\n+    \"1 m\",       # space\n+    \"1x\",        # unknown unit\n+    \"-5s\",       # negative\n+    None,        # None\n+])\n+def test_parse_duration_invalid(bad):\n+    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n+        parse_duration(bad)\ndiff --git a/utils.py b/utils.py\nindex abb3c04..f5f1284 100644\n--- a/utils.py\n+++ b/utils.py\n@@ -3,3 +3,20 @@\n \n def slugify(text):\n     return \"-\".join(text.lower().split())\n+\n+\n+def parse_duration(text):\n+    \"\"\"Return seconds as int for strings like '90s', '15m', '2h'.\n+\n+    Raises ValueError on anything else.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    units = {\"s\": 1, \"m\": 60, \"h\": 3600}\n+    if not text or text[-1] not in units:\n+        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid duration: {text!r}\")\n+    try:\n+        n = int(text[:-1])\n+    except ValueError:\n+        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid duration: {text!r}\")\n+    if n < 0:\n+        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid duration: {text!r}\")\n+    return n * units[text[-1]]\n","text":"Now I'll write the change. Before doing so, I review as the Grump.\n\n---\n\n**Grump Self-Review — planned change**\n\nFiles: `utils.py`, `tests/test_utils.py`\n\n**Planned implementation:**\n\n```python\ndef parse_duration(text):\n    units = {\"s\": 1, \"m\": 60, \"h\": 3600}\n    if not text or text[-1] not in units:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid duration: {text!r}\")\n    try:\n        n = int(text[:-1])\n    except ValueError:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid duration: {text!r}\")\n    return n * units[text[-1]]\n```\n\n**Checklist:**\n\n1. **Scope.** Adds `parse_duration` to `utils.py` and tests to `test_utils.py`. Nothing else touched. Clean.\n\n2. **Inputs.**\n   - `\"90s\"` → 90 ✓\n   - `\"15m\"` → 900 ✓\n   - `\"2h\"` → 7200 ✓\n   - Empty string `\"\"` → `text[-1]` on an empty string raises `IndexError`, not `ValueError`. **Finding:** `not text` check guards this, so `\"\"` → `ValueError`. OK.\n   - `None` → `not text` is truthy for `None`, raises `ValueError`. OK.\n   - Negative: `\"-5s\"` → `int(\"-5\")` = -5, returns -5. Ticket says \"raises `ValueError` on anything else\" — negative numbers are arguably valid integers but produce negative seconds. Ticket doesn't specify; the format `\"-5s\"` isn't one of the listed formats (`90s`, `15m`, `2h`), so I should guard that: add `if n < 0: raise ValueError`. Actually, let me re-read the ticket: \"raises `ValueError` on anything else\" — `-5s` is something else. Guard it.\n   - `\"0s\"` → 0. Not listed but not unreasonable. Leave it.\n   - Oversized: `\"99999999999999999999s\"` → Python handles big ints natively, returns a large int. Fine.\n   - Malformed: `\"1.5m\"` → `int(\"1.5\")` raises `ValueError`, re-raised correctly. ✓\n   - `\"1 m\"` → `int(\"1 \")` raises `ValueError`. ✓\n   - `\"s\"` → `int(\"\")` raises `ValueError`. ✓\n\n3. **Errors.** `ValueError` raised and propagates to caller. No swallowing. ✓\n\n4. **Off-diff.** No schema, config, env vars, permissions touched. ✓\n\n5. **Dependencies.** No new dependencies. ✓\n\n6. **Trust boundaries.** Pure computation, no I/O, no SQL, no secrets. ✓\n\n7. **Tests.** Need: happy path for each unit, `ValueError` on bad input, edge cases (empty string, bad suffix, non-numeric prefix). Must ensure negative values raise `ValueError`.\n\n8. **Rollback.** Pure addition. Revert and deploy is sufficient. ✓\n\n9. **Observability.** N/A — library function. ✓\n\n10. **Naming.** `parse_duration` is clear. ✓\n\n**Finding before writing:** negative numbers (e.g. `\"-5s\"`) would silently return a negative int — that is not a valid duration and the ticket says raise `ValueError` on anything not in the listed forms. Add `n < 0` guard.\n\nNo `BLOCK` findings. Planned verdict after fix: `APPROVE`.\n\n---\n\nNow writing the change with the negative-number guard included:Now I read the final files before the Grump review.---\n\n## Grump Self-Review — final diff\n\nFiles: `utils.py`, `tests/test_utils.py`\n\n**1. Scope.** Ticket: add `parse_duration(text)` to `utils.py`, add tests to `tests/test_utils.py`. Diff adds exactly that. `slugify` and its test are untouched. Nothing extra.\n\n**2. Inputs.**\n- `\"90s\"` → 90 ✓\n- `\"15m\"` → 900 ✓\n- `\"2h\"` → 7200 ✓\n- `\"\"` (empty) → `not text` is `True` at line 14, raises `ValueError`. ✓\n- `None` → `not text` is `True` for `None`, raises `ValueError`. ✓ (`text[-1]` is never reached.)\n- `\"-5s\"` → reaches line 17: `int(\"-5\")` = -5, line 20 guard fires, `ValueError`. ✓\n- `\"m\"` → suffix `\"m\"` in units, then `int(\"\")` raises `ValueError` at line 17, caught and re-raised. ✓\n- `\"1.5m\"` → `int(\"1.5\")` raises `ValueError`, re-raised. ✓\n- `\"1 m\"` → suffix `\"m\"` in units (last char), `int(\"1 \")` raises `ValueError`, re-raised. ✓\n- `\"1x\"` → `\"x\"` not in units, raises `ValueError` at line 15. ✓\n- `\"15\"` → last char `\"5\"` not in units, raises `ValueError`. ✓\n- Oversized integer: Python handles big ints natively, no overflow. ✓\n\n**3. Errors.** Every invalid input raises `ValueError` and propagates to caller. No swallowing, no logging-and-continuing. ✓\n\n**4. Off-diff changes.** No schema, config, env vars, permissions, or shared state touched. ✓\n\n**5. Dependencies.** `pytest` is already used in the project (existing test file). `parse_duration` uses only builtins. ✓\n\n**6. Trust boundaries.** Pure computation. No I/O, no SQL, no secrets, no PII, no network. ✓\n\n**7. Tests.** All three specified units tested at happy path. `ValueError` tested for: empty, no unit, no number, fractional, space, unknown unit, negative, `None`. Tests are at the function boundary, not mocked. ✓\n\n**8. Rollback.** Pure addition. Revert and deploy is sufficient — no migration, no schema change. ✓\n\n**9. Observability.** Library function. N/A. ✓\n\n**10. Naming.** `parse_duration` is unambiguous. `units` dict is clear. No dead code. ✓\n\nNo findings.\n\n```\nGRUMP: APPROVE — utils.py, tests/test_utils.py\n```\n\nFine.","stderr":"","at":"2026-09-05T05:40:06.054Z"}
