em, so this is not a finding under the protocol.\n\n**8. Rollback.** Pure additive change to a function signature with a default — existing callers continue to work unchanged. Revert + deploy is sufficient.\n\n**9. Observability.** No logging added or removed; no change in observability posture.\n\n**10. Naming and dead code.** `tags` is an accurate name. No dead code introduced.\n\n---\n\n**Mutable-default-argument check:** I will use `tags=None` and assign `[]` inside the body to avoid the classic Python mutable-default-argument bug where every call without `tags` would share the same list object.\n\n```\nGRUMP: APPROVE — reports.py\nFine.\n```---\n\n## Grump self-review (post-edit)\n\n**1. Scope.** `build_report` gains `tags=None`; returned dict gains `\"tags\"` list. Nothing else changed. Matches ticket exactly.\n\n**2. Inputs.** `tags` absent → `None` → `[]`, a fresh list. `tags=[]` → `list([])` → `[]`. `tags=[\"a\",\"b\"]` → `[\"a\",\"b\"]`. `tags=None` explicit → `[]`. No mutable default argument. Caller-supplied iterable is copied via `list(...)` so the caller mutating their original list does not affect the returned dict.\n\n**3. Errors.** `list(tags)` will raise `TypeError` if `tags` is not iterable (e.g. an integer). The ticket specifies `tags` is a list; this is the same trust posture as `name` (no validation). Not a finding — the ticket does not ask for it and we cannot name a production path where an integer arrives here.\n\n**4. Off-diff.** None.\n\n**5. Dependencies.** None.\n\n**6. Trust boundaries.** No boundary crossed.\n\n**7. Tests.** No tests in repo; ticket doesn't ask.\n\n**8. Rollback.** Additive; existing callers pass zero arguments and now get `\"tags\": []`. No migration needed.\n\n**9. Observability.** No change.\n\n**10. Naming.** Clean.\n\n```\nGRUMP: APPROVE — reports.py\nFine.\n```","stderr":"","at":"2026-09-05T06:08:50.297Z"}
