lt; existing callers unaffected. Revert is clean.\n\n**9. Observability.** No logging added or removed; nothing to observe here.\n\n**10. Naming/dead code.** `tags` is the name the ticket specifies. Clean.\n\n**Verdict (pre-write):** No findings. APPROVE — [`reports.py`](reports.py).\n\n```\nGRUMP: APPROVE — reports.py\nFine.\n```\n\nNow making the call:## Grump self-review (post-write)\n\n**1. Scope.** Change adds `tags=None` parameter and `\"tags\"` list to the returned dict. Nothing else touched. Matches ticket exactly.\n\n**2. Inputs.**\n- `tags` absent: `None` → `[]` in output. ✓\n- `tags=None` explicit: same. ✓\n- `tags=[]`: `list([])` → `[]`. ✓\n- `tags=[\"a\",\"b\"]`: `list([\"a\",\"b\"])` → fresh copy. ✓\n- Mutable default argument trap avoided by using `None` sentinel. ✓\n- Non-iterable passed (e.g. `tags=42`): `list(42)` raises `TypeError` at the call site — correct fail-fast behaviour; the function makes no promise about non-iterable input.\n\n**3. Errors.** No new swallowed exceptions.\n\n**4. Off-diff changes.** None.\n\n**5. Dependencies.** None.\n\n**6. Trust boundaries.** None crossed.\n\n**7. Tests.** No test infrastructure exists in the repo; ticket did not request tests.\n\n**8. Rollback.** Existing callers pass only `name`; the new parameter has a default. Revert is a one-line change with no migration.\n\n**9. Observability.** Nothing to observe.\n\n**10. Naming/dead code.** `tags` matches the ticket's own language. No dead code.\n\n```\nGRUMP: APPROVE — reports.py\nFine.\n```","stderr":"","at":"2026-09-05T06:09:11.276Z"}
