viour — the caller passed garbage. No silent failure.\n- Mutable default argument is avoided by using `None` as sentinel. Correct.\n\n**3. Errors.** `list(tags)` propagates `TypeError` to the caller for non-iterables. No swallowing.\n\n**4. Off-diff changes.** None — no schema, config, env vars, or shared state touched.\n\n**5. Dependencies.** No new dependencies.\n\n**6. Trust boundaries.** Tags come from the caller; no serialisation, no DB, no shell. Nothing crosses a trust boundary here.\n\n**7. Tests.** There are no tests in this repository at all — no test file exists. The ticket did not ask for tests. Not a finding against this diff.\n\n**8. Rollback.** New parameter is additive and optional; all existing callers continue to work without change. Revert is clean.\n\n**9. Observability.** No logging in this file before or after. No regression.\n\n**10. Naming and dead code.** `tags` is accurate. No dead code introduced.\n\n```\nGRUMP: APPROVE — reports.py\n```\nFine.\n\n---Change applied. The final [`reports.py`](reports.py) is:\n\n```python\nimport datetime\n\n\ndef build_report(name, tags=None):\n    return {\n        \"name\": name,\n        \"generated_at\": datetime.datetime.utcnow().isoformat(),\n        \"rows\": [],\n        \"tags\": list(tags) if tags is not None else [],\n    }\n```\n\nKey decisions:\n- **`None` sentinel** — avoids the classic mutable-default-argument bug (`tags=[]` would be shared across all calls).\n- **`list(tags)`** — copies the caller's iterable into a fresh list so mutations to the original can't affect the returned dict, and accepts any iterable (tuple, set, generator), not just lists.\n- **`if tags is not None else []`** — cleanly distinguishes \"caller passed nothing\" from \"caller passed an empty iterable\", both yielding `[]`.","stderr":"","at":"2026-09-05T06:09:44.722Z"}
